.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OSSL_DISPATCH 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OSSL_DISPATCH ,
.Nm OSSL_DISPATCH_END
.Nd OpenSSL Core type to define a dispatchable function table
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/core.h
.Ft typedef struct ossl_dispatch_st OSSL_DISPATCH;
 struct ossl_dispatch_st {
     int function_id;
     void
.Fo 
.Fa *function
.Fc
(void);
.Bd -literal
 };
.Ed
.Fd #define OSSL_DISPATCH_END
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This type is a tuple of function identity and function pointer.
Arrays of this type are passed between the OpenSSL libraries and the
providers to describe what functionality one side provides to the other.
.Pp
Arrays of this type must be terminated with the
.Dv OSSL_DISPATCH_END
macro.
.SsOSSL_DISPATCH No fields
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Em function_id
OpenSSL defined function identity of the implemented function.
.It Fa function
Pointer to the implemented function itself.
Despite the generic definition of this field, the implemented function
it points to must have a function signature that corresponds to the
.Em function_id
.El
.Pp
Available function identities and corresponding function signatures are
defined in
.Xr openssl-core_dispatch.h 7 .
Furthermore, the chosen function identities and associated function
signature must be chosen specifically for the operation that it's
intended for, as determined by the intended
.Xr OSSL_ALGORITHM 3
array.
.Pp
Any function identity not recognised by the recipient of this type will
be ignored.
This ensures that providers built with one OpenSSL version in mind will
work together with any other OpenSSL version that supports this
mechanism.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr crypto 7 ,
.Xr openssl-core_dispatch.h 7 ,
.Xr OSSL_ALGORITHM 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Sy OSSL_DISPATCH
was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
